{"availability":"available","full":"brianketchens/ercot-predictive-modelling","name":"ercot-predictive-modelling","description":"The project runs in two phases. Phase 1 establishes a high-accuracy baseline using autoregressive load lags. Phase 2 deliberately removes those lags and rebuilds the model as a weather-structural forecaster — trading a few points of headline R² for a physically interpretable model that can answer scenario questions a persistence model cannot.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-07T20:18:56Z","updated":"2026-07-11T11:29:07Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ercot-predictive-modelling-pzanfe9eeappdcuqskncsn9.streamlit.app/","topics":["ingestion-pipeline","python","streamlit","tableau-dashboards"],"demo":"https://ercot-predictive-modelling-pzanfe9eeappdcuqskncsn9.streamlit.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.750Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.750Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.750Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.750Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An end-to-end machine learning and data engineering pipeline that ingests a full decade (2016–2025) of historical grid load and localized hourly weather data to forecast energy demand in the ERCOT Houston (Coast) region.","The project runs in two phases. Phase 1 establishes a high-accuracy baseline using autoregressive load lags. Phase 2 deliberately removes those lags and rebuilds the model as a weather-structural forecaster — trading a few points of headline R² for a physically interpretable model that can answer scenario questions a persistence model cannot."],"features":["Phase 2 transforms raw temporal and weather observations into 22 physically-grounded demand indicators. Notably, it contains no autoregressive load lags — every feature is an exogenous driver available ahead of time,…","Realized thermodynamic load (humidex): Combines air temperature and dew point into a single felt-heat index, capturing the compounding effect of humidity on cooling demand.","Effective solar penetration (effectivesolargain): Direct normal irradiance attenuated by cloud cover, modeling actual solar heat gain on buildings.","Kinetic wind cooling (kineticcoolingindex): Temperature discounted by wind speed, since moving air changes the effective cooling load.","Thermal adaptation (thermalshockdelta): Temperature minus its trailing 7-day mean, capturing demand response to sudden swings rather than absolute levels."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brianketchens/ercot-predictive-modelling/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e7da17aef42914d0908702e9b57a28d1dd2712f0696e266bf8cc2bfd95b67ebf","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.954Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.954Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An end-to-end machine learning and data engineering pipeline that ingests a full decade (2016–2025) of historical grid load and localized hourly weather data to forecast energy demand in the ERCOT Houston (Coast) region.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brianketchens/ercot-predictive-modelling/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"e7da17aef42914d0908702e9b57a28d1dd2712f0696e266bf8cc2bfd95b67ebf","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brianketchens/ercot-predictive-modelling/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.954Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-07-11T11:29:07Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brianketchens/ercot-predictive-modelling/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.955Z","hash":"e7da17aef42914d0908702e9b57a28d1dd2712f0696e266bf8cc2bfd95b67ebf","originalBytes":11453,"storedBytes":11453,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["model","load","phase","data","weather","ercot","feature","hourly","demand","grid","lags","baseline","cooling","peak","pipeline","src","autoregressive"